Source: ps3-spu
Section: misc
Priority: optional
Maintainer: PS3 Linux project <ps3@localhost>
Build-Depends: debhelper-compat (= 13)
Standards-Version: 4.7.2
Rules-Requires-Root: no

Package: ps3-spu
Architecture: ppc64
Depends: ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends}
Recommends: ps3-spu-programs
Description: SPU program runner and libspeq tools for the PS3's Cell SPEs
 spurun loads and runs an SPU program through spufs; speq-dxt tests and benchmarks libspeq's
 DXT1 texture encoder; speq-bench measures libspeq's queue (wake and completion latency,
 parking, the 0x2104 syscall path, the decrementer, DMA bandwidth) with bench.spu. The
 package loads spufs at boot and mounts it at /spu.

Package: ps3-spu-programs
Architecture: all
Depends: ${misc:Depends}
Breaks: ps3-spu (<< ${source:Version})
Replaces: ps3-spu (<< ${source:Version})
Description: SPU programs for the PS3
 SPU programs (*.spu, built with spu-elf GCC) in /usr/lib/ps3/spu: hello.spu, run with
 spurun; bench.spu, libspeq's resident worker with the operations speq-bench uses; and
 dxt.spu, the worker libspeq's DXT1 texture compression runs on the SPEs.

Package: libspeq0
Section: libs
Architecture: ppc64
Multi-Arch: same
Depends: ps3-spu, ps3-spu-programs (= ${source:Version}), ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends}
Description: work queues on the PS3's SPEs, and DXT1 texture compression
 libspeq runs jobs on resident SPU workers fed through spufs, and provides services built on
 them. The first is S3TC DXT1 texture compression, which Mesa loads at run time
 (speq_s3tc_compress_v1). It runs van Waveren's real-time DXT1 on the SPEs (dxt.spu), and
 on the PPE for small images or when no SPE is available, with the same output.
 SPEQ_S3TC=auto|spu|ppe|off chooses the encoder, SPEQ_DEBUG=1 logs each call.

Package: libspeq-dev
Section: libdevel
Architecture: ppc64
Multi-Arch: same
Depends: libspeq0 (= ${binary:Version}), ${misc:Depends}
Description: work queues on the PS3's SPEs (development files)
 The header speq.h and the libspeq.so link for building against libspeq.
